  "configuration_id": "config_040",
  "reason": "The current best (config_027, acc=0.706) uses scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted. The largest single gain in this search came from switching the RNA encoder from pca_n2000 to scvi_n200 (+0.071 accuracy). config_040 tests whether scgpt—a more powerful, generative RNA encoder—can push accuracy further while keeping all other settings at their proven-optimal values (imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile). This is the highest-information experiment: if scgpt beats scvi_n200, it opens a new promising direction for the remaining 3 experiments; if it underperforms, it confirms scvi_n200 is the best RNA encoder and focuses remaining budget on aggregation/fusion refinements. Expected cost is moderate (~5–7 GPU hours), comparable to config_027 (4.82) since scgpt is a similar-scale encoder to scvi_n200 and the image/aggregation pipeline is identical."
}

